    </header>

    <main>
      <!-- ============ HERO ============ -->
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="hero-inner">
          <h1 class="hero-title">freemkv-fw</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">
            <strong>freemkv-fw</strong> turns any stock MediaTek image into
            freemkv firmware — re-signed so the drive accepts it — and
            verifies a file or a live drive.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- ============ CREATE ============ -->
      <section class="block">
        <div class="section-inner">
          <span class="kicker">Create</span>
          <h2 class="section-title">freemkv-fw create</h2>

          <div class="terminal">
            <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="dot dot-r"></span><span class="dot dot-y"></span><span class="dot dot-g"></span>
              <span class="terminal-title">freemkv-fw create</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="terminal-body"><code><span class="c"># One input, one output — freemkv-fw auto-detects the model</span>
<span class="p">$</span> freemkv-fw create BU40N_1.00.bin BU40N_1.00.freemkv.bin

<span class="c">freemkv-fw 0.4.0 — detected LG BU40N · base 1.00</span>

  Identity ................. <span class="ok">added</span>
  Speed .................... <span class="ok">added</span>
  Volume ID (VID) .......... <span class="ok">added</span>
  Bus Encryption ........... <span class="ok">added</span>
  Region-free .............. <span class="ok">added</span>
  Diagnostic Dump .......... <span class="ok">added</span>

<span class="c">Downgrade-enable (DE) byte ... set (flashes over any version)</span>
<span class="c">Re-signing integrity table ... ok</span>
<span class="c">Wrote BU40N_1.00.freemkv.bin (2,097,152 bytes)</span></code></pre>
          </div>

          <div class="grid cap-grid">
            {fwCapabilities.map((c) => (
              <div class="cap-item" data-status={c.status}>
                <span class={`cap-dot cap-dot-${c.status}`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <div class="cap-body">
                  <span class="cap-name">
                    {c.name}
                    {c.status === 'wip' && <span class="cap-wip">WIP</span>}
                  </span>
                  <span class="cap-detail">{c.detail}</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))}
          </div>

          <p class="block-note">
            Every build sets the <strong>downgrade-enable (DE) byte</strong>, so a
            freemkv image installs <strong>over any existing firmware version</strong> —
            newer OEM or MK — instead of being blocked by the drive's anti-rollback.
            (Proven on hardware: with DE set the drive accepts a lower version; with it
            cleared the same downgrade is rejected and nothing is written.)
          </p>
          <p class="block-note">
            <code>create</code> auto-detects the model from the image. The
            drive stays stock until the freemkv command is knocked. See the
            <a href="/docs/firmware-tools/#command-reference">full command reference</a> for
            exactly what each capability rides.
          </p>

          <h2 class="section-title subhead" id="verify">freemkv-fw verify</h2>
          <p class="section-lead">
            <code>verify</code> answers one question two ways: point it at a
            <strong>file</strong> to check the firmware's own integrity, or at
            a <strong>live drive</strong> (e.g. <code>/dev/sg0</code>) to ask
            the drive directly and report what it says back.
          </p>

          <div class="terminal">
            <div class="terminal-bar" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="dot dot-r"></span><span class="dot dot-y"></span><span class="dot dot-g"></span>
              <span class="terminal-title">freemkv-fw verify</span>
            </div>
            <pre class="terminal-body"><code><span class="c"># File verify — checks the image's own integrity table</span>
<span class="p">$</span> freemkv-fw verify BU40N_1.00.freemkv.bin
<span class="ok">ok</span> — integrity table valid, freemkv capabilities present

<span class="c"># Live verify — asks the drive itself</span>
<span class="p">$</span> freemkv-fw verify /dev/sg0
<span class="ok">freemkv detected</span> — drive answered the identity check</code></pre>
          </div>

          <p class="section-lead cmd-teaser">
            Every freemkv-fw command rides a single knocked
            <code>READ BUFFER</code> — the drive stays 100% OEM until
            activated, and every toggle is designed to be reversible without
            reflashing.
            <a href="/docs/firmware-tools/#command-reference">Firmware command reference →</a>
          </p>

          <div class="grid dl-grid">
            {platforms.map((p) => (
              <article class="card" data-os={p.os}>
                <h3 class="card-title">{p.name}</h3>
                <div class="dl-list">
